# Resolve only releases published at least two days ago, so a hijacked publish is usually found
# and pulled before an install here picks it up. It applies when npm chooses a version: npm
# install, npm update, npm audit fix. npm 11.21.1 and 12.2.1 enforce it; npm 10.9.9, which Node 22
# bundles, ignores the key without a warning, so on Node 22 nothing enforces it. npm ci installs
# the lockfile's exact versions and never checks their age; the Dependabot cooldown is what keeps
# a new release out of the lockfile. scripts/supply-chain-check.ts fails while this is missing or
# set below two days.
min-release-age=2
